# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Secrets -- never commit credentials
.env
.env.*
# ...but DO commit the templates (they carry keys + guidance, never values).
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Stray nested git repo accidentally left in the tree (README-only, has its own
# .git) — never part of the app; keep it out of this repository entirely.
job track/

# Logs
*.log
server-restart.log

# Runtime artifacts (regenerated / user-uploaded at runtime)
uploads/
storage/

# Local automation artifacts + datasets (kept on disk, NOT part of the app):
# the n8n export, the Make.com import blueprints, and the seed/reference CSVs.
*.blueprint.json
My workflow*.json
*_datasets.csv

# Claude Code session files and worktrees.
#
# `.claude/*` rather than `.claude/` on purpose: git does not descend into an
# excluded DIRECTORY, so a later `!.claude/skills/` would never be evaluated.
# Excluding the CONTENTS instead leaves the directory itself readable, which is
# what makes the negation below work.
.claude/*

# The architecture skill IS project documentation and belongs in version
# control -- it is the reference used for the system proposal and technical
# defence. Keeping it untracked meant a clone or a fresh worktree silently had
# no copy, and the only version was whatever sat on one developer's machine.
!.claude/skills/

# Custom subagents are project tooling (e.g. the architecture guardian) and belong
# in version control too, so a clone gets them — same rationale as the skill above.
!.claude/agents/

# Everything else under .claude/ stays out: worktrees are checkouts of this same
# repository, and session state is per-machine noise.
.claude/worktrees/
